KZ3 patch 1073 (SPU pass 57, default on; KZ3_TS_CREATE_OLD=1 = the old updates): cellSpursCreateTask updates the
taskset's enabled and ready bitsets atomically. They share one 128-byte line with the SPU task library
(GETLLAR/PUTLLC) and with the host task exit (spu_taskset_task_exited, under the lock-line lock since patch 1030),
but CreateTask set them with a plain word read-modify-write (spurs_bitset_set). A task exit clearing its enabled bit
between that read and write was undone: the task's enabled bit came back with no task behind it (ready 0, exit entry
state 2), so cellSpursJoinTask2 on that id never returned. KZ3: Havok task 0 of the physics pool, reused ids 1-4 for
every later step, and the pool destructor at quit-to-menu (T7) waited for task 0 forever. Real libsre updates the
bitsets in a lock-line reservation loop. Now the free-id search sets the enabled bit (reserving the id) and the ready
bit is set after task_info is written, each under the line's stripe lock with raw byte access, followed by the
reservation kill (spu_coh_notify_write). spurs_taskset_write_task_info writes task_info without touching the bitsets.
Host test tools/spu/test_ts_create_race.sh.

--- a/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
@@ -1181,6 +1181,54 @@
  * from an EA computed out of r3 = that argument (spu_0003 task main @0x17e70:
  * `wrch $ch18, f(r3.word3)`), so a zero argument makes it GET from EA 0 and
  * stall. lsPattern/argument arrive as guest EAs (generic adapter forwards r3..r10). */
+/* KZ3 patch 1073: cellSpursCreateTask's bitset updates as atomic line updates. The taskset's ready/pending/enabled
+ * bitsets (+0x10/+0x20/+0x30) share one 128-byte line with the SPU-side task library (GETLLAR/PUTLLC) and with the
+ * task exit (spu_taskset_task_exited, under the lock-line lock since patch 1030). CreateTask used a plain word
+ * read-modify-write (spurs_bitset_set: vm_read32 | mask, vm_write32): a task exit clearing its enabled bit between
+ * the read and the write was undone. KZ3 T7: Havok task 0 exited (exit entry state 2, ready 0) while the PPU created
+ * the next step's tasks 1-4 in the same byte; its enabled bit came back, no thread owned it, every later step used ids
+ * 1-4, and the pool destructor's cellSpursJoinTask2(ts, 0) waited for it forever (SPU pass 57, KZ3_JOIN2_PROBE dump).
+ * Real libsre updates the bitsets with a lock-line reservation loop, so a concurrent change is never lost and SPU
+ * reservations on the line are broken. Here: the free-id search and the enabled bit (reserving the id), then the ready
+ * bit after task_info is written, each under the line's stripe lock with raw byte access (vm_write32 would take the
+ * same non-recursive lock), ending with the reservation kill. KZ3_TS_CREATE_OLD=1 = the old unlocked updates. */
+/* kz3-ts-create begin (tools/spu/test_ts_create_race.sh compiles this block) */
+static int kz3_ts_create_old(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (v < 0) { const char* e = getenv("KZ3_TS_CREATE_OLD"); v = (e && *e == '1'); }
+    return v;
+}
+/* Find the first clear enabled bit and set it, atomically; CELL_SPURS_MAX_TASK when all 128 are taken. */
+static u32 kz3_ts_take_slot(uint32_t ts)
+{
+    u32 slot = CELL_SPURS_MAX_TASK;
+    if (kz3_ts_create_old()) {
+        for (u32 t = 0; t < CELL_SPURS_MAX_TASK; t++)
+            if (!(vm_read8(ts + 0x30 + t / 8) & (0x80u >> (t % 8)))) { slot = t; break; }
+        return slot;
+    }
+    const uint64_t m = spu_ll_mask(ts + 0x30, 16);
+    spu_ll_lock_mask(m);
+    uint8_t* en = vm_base + ts + 0x30;
+    for (u32 t = 0; t < CELL_SPURS_MAX_TASK; t++)
+        if (!(en[t / 8] & (0x80u >> (t % 8)))) { en[t / 8] |= (uint8_t)(0x80u >> (t % 8)); slot = t; break; }
+    if (slot < CELL_SPURS_MAX_TASK) spu_coh_notify_write(ts + 0x30);
+    spu_ll_unlock_mask(m);
+    return slot;
+}
+/* Set bit id of the bitset at ts+off (0x10 ready, 0x30 enabled), atomically. */
+static void kz3_ts_set_bit(uint32_t ts, uint32_t off, u32 id)
+{
+    if (kz3_ts_create_old()) { spurs_bitset_set(ts + off, id); return; }
+    const uint64_t m = spu_ll_mask(ts + off, 16);
+    spu_ll_lock_mask(m);
+    vm_base[ts + off + id / 8] |= (uint8_t)(0x80u >> (id % 8));
+    spu_coh_notify_write(ts + off);
+    spu_ll_unlock_mask(m);
+}
+/* kz3-ts-create end */
+
 s32 cellSpursCreateTask(CellSpursTaskset* taskset, CellSpursTaskId* taskId,
                         void* elf, void* context, u32 sizeContext,
                         u32 lsPattern_ea, u32 argument_ea)
